  ],
  "description": "BBE 482i engaged channel B, based on the 2004 Farrand board analysis and New Japan Radio NJM2153 data. The pseudo state-variable filter, summing amplifier, Process and Lo Contour retain the source-board values. The high-band stage uses a finite-bandwidth peak detector, the documented series 3.32 kΩ/0.22 µF detector branch and separate 2.2 µF integration capacitor. A continuous diode-limited gain curve reproduces the published level dependence approximately. Detector charge and recovery paths are functional estimates of the proprietary chip. TL072 sections represent its amplifiers. LED meters and bypass are outside this model.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Lo Contour",
      "Process"
    ]
  },
  "name": "BBE 482i Sonic Maximizer Channel B",
  "outputNode": "out",
  "version": 3,
  "wires": [
    {
      "points": [
        {
          "x": 23,
          "y": 37
        },
        {
          "x": 27,
